<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 10_flexbox/15: Reordering with order -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Reordering with order</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .row { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; background: #e0e7ff; padding: 0.5rem; border-radius: 10px; min-height: 8rem; }
    .row div { background: #6366f1; color: #fff; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; }
    .first { order: -1; background: #ec4899; }
    .last { order: 99; background: #10b981; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Reordering with order</h1>
    <p class="lead">order changes the visual order without touching the HTML.</p>
    <div class="row"><div>One</div><div class="last">Two (order: 99)</div><div>Three</div><div class="first">Four (order: -1)</div></div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
